      "exampleTransliteration": "adrusu fī l-jāmiʿati",
      "exampleEnglish": "I study at the university.",
      "grammarNote": "درس is back to Form I, but with the DAMMA stem-vowel pattern (yadrusu) instead of the fatha pattern you've mostly seen (yadhhabu, yaʿmalu) — the same pattern as كتب/يكتب. Its imperative would follow the same damma-prosthetic rule as اُكْتُبْ: اُدْرُسْ, though it isn't drilled here. No new nouns this level — فِي الْجَامِعَةِ reuses level 13's noun directly.",
